Drivezzz Source Licence, version 1.0 (11 November 2026)

Copyright (c) 2026 s3rver. Everything this licence doesn't give you stays with s3rver.

Drivezzz's code is public so that anyone can read it, check it, learn from it and
build something of their own on it, with their own smart contract if they like.
What you may not do is copy it: put Drivezzz out again, as it is, or with only its
name, look or settings changed.

So this is a source-available licence, not an open-source licence as the Open
Source Initiative defines it: building on the code is allowed, copying it is not.


1. Words used here

"The Software" is everything in this repository that s3rver made: the iPhone and
Android apps, the server, the admin panel, the website, the escrow program in
contract/, and the tests, scripts and documents. Parts made by others keep their
own licence (section 8).

"Your own work" is something you made with the Software, or with parts of it, that
you changed in substance, so that it is a product of your own and not Drivezzz
with another coat of paint: it adds, removes or reworks what it does or how it
works.

"A copy" is the Software, or anything made from it that isn't your own work:
Drivezzz as it is, or with only its name, logo, colours, texts, translations,
keys, addresses, servers, prices, fees or other settings changed, or with only
small fixes.

"Publish" is making something available to anyone outside your own organisation:
in an app store, on a website, as a download, as a service people use, or by
handing it over.

"You" is the person or organisation using this licence.


2. What you may do

For free, worldwide, for as long as you keep to this licence, you may:

a. Read, study, run and test the Software, and change it, for yourself or inside
   your own organisation. That includes running your own server and apps to
   develop and test with.

b. Make your own work, and publish it, run it as a service and sell it, under
   your own name.

c. Have your own smart contract: deploy the escrow program in contract/, changed
   or not, as a program of your own, with your own keys, program ID and fee
   address, on any network, and use it in your own work. It is then yours to run
   and to look after.

d. Use parts of the Software, such as a file, a function, the escrow program or
   the end-to-end encryption, in another product of your own.

e. Keep a public fork of this repository on GitHub, or a similar site, with this
   licence and notice in it, to work towards your own work or towards a change
   you send back.


3. What you may not do

a. Publish a copy. That includes putting Drivezzz, or an app or server that is a
   copy of it, in an app store, on a website or online as a service.

b. Use the name Drivezzz, its logo or app icon, or anything else that makes people
   think your work is Drivezzz, or comes from or is approved by s3rver. Give your
   work its own name and look. You may say it is "based on Drivezzz" and link to
   this repository.

c. Remove or change the copyright notice or this licence in the parts you use.

d. Use the Software, or your own work, with Drivezzz's own servers, services,
   accounts, users or escrow, unless s3rver agreed to it in writing. This licence
   is about the code, not the Drivezzz service: the Terms and the End User Licence
   Agreement at https://drivezzz.s3rver.nl cover the service and its app.

e. Use the Software against the law, or to deceive or harm people.


4. When you publish your own work

a. Say in it, where people can find it (its about page, website or README), that
   it is based on Drivezzz, with a link to https://github.com/1arrcy1/Drivezzz.

b. The parts that came from the Software stay under this licence, also inside
   your work: whoever gets them from you gets them under this licence. Your own
   changes and additions you may license as you like.

c. You are responsible for your own work: for its users, for the money and the
   escrow it handles, and for following the law where it runs. s3rver has no
   part in it.


5. Sending changes back

If you send a change to this repository, as a pull request, a patch or code in an
issue, you allow s3rver to use, change and publish it in Drivezzz under any
licence, and everyone else to use it under this licence. You confirm that you
have the right to give that.


6. No guarantees

The Software is given as it is, without any guarantee, as far as the law allows.
It moves money on a blockchain. The escrow program has had no paid security
audit, and a bug can lock or misroute money. If you run it, or anything made
from it, you do so at your own risk.


7. No liability

As far as the law allows, s3rver isn't liable for any damage from using the
Software, or from not being able to use it.


8. Parts made by others

Some parts come from others and have their own licence, which applies to those
parts and which this licence doesn't limit:

- NFCPassportReader (MIT): drivezzz/Features/Checks/NFCPassportReader-LICENSE.txt
- The SFace face model (Apache 2.0): drivezzz/Features/Checks/SFace-LICENSE.txt
- On Android, JMRTD and SCUBA (LGPL 2.1), Bouncy Castle (MIT), MapLibre
  (BSD 2-Clause) and others: android/app/src/main/assets/licences/
- The CSCA master list in server/src/csca/, published by Germany's BSI.

The packages the apps, the server and the escrow program load (Swift packages,
Gradle, npm and Cargo) come with their own licences too.


9. Ending

If you break this licence, it ends for you. If you stop and put it right within
30 days after s3rver tells you, it comes back. That happens once: a second time,
it ends for good.


10. The law

Dutch law applies to this licence. Disputes go to the competent court in the
Netherlands.


11. Anything else

Want to do something this licence doesn't allow, such as publishing a copy, or
connecting your own work to Drivezzz's servers? Ask: info@s3rver.nl.
